{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Living the Dream", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Keep on Dreaming", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Tag Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tag questions</span> are used to ask for clarification and confirmation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Tag questions are short questions that come at the end of statements.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They are used when we want to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">confirm whether or not something is true</span></li><li><span class=\"strong\">  to encourage a response </span>from someone we are talking to.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li vale=\"1\">A <span class=\"strong\">positive </span>statement comes before a <span class=\"strong\">negative </span>question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'yes'. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were </span>stressed, <span class=\"strong\">weren't </span>you?</li><li> You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> looking for work, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you? </li><li> She<span class=\"strong\"> has </span>a degree, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't </span>she? </li><li> He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak Spanish, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</li></ul></span></li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">A <span class=\"strong\">negative </span> statement comes before a <span class=\"strong\">positive </span> question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'no'. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li> You <span class=\"strong\">weren't </span> stressed, <span class=\"strong\"> were </span>you?</li> <li> You <span class=\"strong\">aren't </span> looking for work, <span class=\"strong\"> are </span> you? </li> <li> She <span class=\"strong\"> doesn't </span> have a degree, <span class=\"strong\"> does </span> she? </li><li> He <span class=\"strong\"> can't </span> speak Spanish, <span class=\"strong\"> can </span> he? </li></ul></span></li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, the tag will use the same verb. For the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> the tag will be the auxiliary verb <span class=\"strong\">have </span> or <span class=\"strong\">has</span>. For all other main verbs, use the tag <span class=\"italic\"> do/does/don't/doesn't </span> or <span class=\"italic\"> did/didn't</span>. Look at the examples in the chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":13,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I am\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't I?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"haven't I?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hasn't she?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "So, you aren't working yet, are you? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That is a publishing house, isn't it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You've heard of them, haven't you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You talked to them, didn't you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm the boss, aren't I?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Reported Speech and Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">reported speech</span> when you are saying (reporting)  what other people said. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">reported speech</span> when we want to repeat what someone had previously said. </br>You need to change the verb to the next past form. This is called backsliding. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Direct speech </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Reported speech </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Robert: \\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">worked </span> there\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> had worked</span> there.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Kelly: \\\"I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m coming </span>to lunch.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She said she <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> was coming </span> to lunch.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Co-workers: \\\"We <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> finished</span>.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" They said they <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had </span>finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Mark: \\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can </span> type.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> could </span> type.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Mindy: \\\"Where do you <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> study</span>?\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She asked me where I <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> studied</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You have to change the <span class=\"strong\">pronoun</span> if you are reporting what someone else said. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\"<ul> <li> I said, \"I don't want to go.\" > I said <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I </span> </span> didn't want to go. </li><li> Tina said, \"I don't want to go.\" > Tina said <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> she </span> </span> didn't want to go.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What do you mean where have I been?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What did they say?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The director said that they are going to hire an editor assistant and they liked my qualifications.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My friend Davis heard that BFP had a good standing as an up-and-coming company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you want to <span class=\"strong\">report questions</span> asked, the <span class=\"strong\">subject </span> normally comes before the <span class=\"strong\">verb</span>. <br> Example: <br> Direct: \"Where are they?\" <br> Indirect: He asked me where they were.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When the question is a yes/no question, you use <span class=\"strong\">if</span> or <span class=\"strong\">whether </span> to report it. <br> Example: <br> Direct: \"Is that the report?\" <br> Indirect: She asked me if that was the report. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They asked whether there was a new editor hired yet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The interviewer asked me when I had graduated from school.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sounds like a plan", "type": "name"}, {"content": "that's a good idea", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  <br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Let's meet Thursday? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Bianca</span>: Sounds like a plan.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you are gathering information about a company.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "up-and-coming", "type": "name"}, {"content": "promising; has a lot of potential for growth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My friend Davis heard that BFP is an up-and-coming company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "good standing", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a solid or well-established position compared to others", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  BFP has a good standing in the publishing world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "by the way", "type": "name"}, {"content": " an expression showing you are about to give an additional piece of related information", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  By the way, Adam always asks what you have been doing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lend a hand", "type": "name"}, {"content": "help", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Adam is going to lend a hand as well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I visit employment websites and search them efficiently.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I analyze information and compare it to the criteria (my job skills).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a description of why this job could be suitable for me.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I compare my ideas and give feedback.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Visit a popular employment website to search for positions. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Put in a few keywords for jobs that you would like. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose two jobs from the list of positions you have found that you would like to apply for. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you can't find one then create your own job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make sure to choose jobs that match your skills in some way. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The jobs do not need to be identical to the jobs you have had in the past, or to the subject you are studying at school. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a paragraph for each job explaining why those jobs would match your skill set. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare with a partner and give feedback.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can ask for confirmation. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can discuss future plans.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can report what someone had previously said.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How many job interviews have you been to?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What kinds of questions did they ask you?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Preparing for a job interview!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Maybe one of your co-workers has a car you can borrow. You should <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">ask around</span>.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "To <span class=\"italic\">\"ask around\"</span> means to ask  a number of people for information or advice.", "tip_id": 0, "type": "text"}], "type": "tips"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "MMM", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "I am going to go to a place called BFP for an interview.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"text": "", "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "I think I like my chances there.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}, {"text": "", "correct": true, "_data": [{"content": "I am going to take this week to prepare.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 2}, {"text": "", "correct": true, "_data": [{"content": "He is going to be interviewing for jobs soon.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 3}, {"text": "", "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "He needs some practice as well.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 4}, {"text": "", "correct": true, "_data": [{"content": "I will see you on Thursday though.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 5}, {"text": "", "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "I was in the bathroom scrubbing my hands.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 6}, {"text": "", "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "They sent an e-mail.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 7}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "Which of the following sentences talks about the future?", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "secondary_1", "type": "obj